# Renders as "Cite this repository" on the GitHub sidebar, and is what a
# reference manager reads when someone imports this repo.
#
# When a Zenodo DOI is minted, add it under identifiers and set `doi:` so the
# citation points at a fixed, archived version rather than a moving branch.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Original-data research datasets and measurement harness, sujitkarki.com.np
message: If you use these datasets, please cite them.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Karki
    given-names: Sujit
    website: https://www.sujitkarki.com.np
version: 2026.09.0
date-released: "2026-09-08"
repository-code: https://github.com/Sujit-karki/sujit-blog
url: https://www.sujitkarki.com.np/research
abstract: >-
  Datasets behind the original-data posts on sujitkarki.com.np, published with
  the code that produced them and the raw rows behind every figure. Covers
  local language models used as measurement instruments (numeracy, progressive
  tax, a paired named-versus-anonymous account-choice study, an advice
  benchmark published with its failed scoring metrics, and energy per million
  tokens on consumer hardware), figures computed from published formulas and
  government series, and values extracted from primary documents including SEC
  filings, privacy policies and cryptocurrency whitepapers. Failed and
  contended runs are included as evidence rather than discarded.
keywords:
  - local language models
  - benchmark
  - reproducibility
  - personal finance
  - Ollama
  - SEC filings
  - consumer price index
  - readability
  - data journalism
  - open data
